Version 0.3

- Added `mark_published.py`: tags uploaded files Published (green) and removes
  Approved for Publishing in Finder, from upload_log.json; separate from the
  YouTube code. `launchd/install_mark_published.sh` runs it every 6 hours
- Thumbnails: optional `thumbnail:` in both YAML files. The uploader sets them
  after processing finishes and retries unset ones on the next run
- Switched from the deprecated oauth2client to google-auth; removed the unrelated
  `apiclient` package and unused `pycurl`/`http-client` from requirements
- One shared sign-in (`token.json`) for both scripts; expired Testing-mode sign-ins
  reopen the browser instead of failing
- Uploader: `--vids` now works (it was ignored)
- Uploader: validates every entry before uploading anything; missing filename no longer crashes
- Uploader: records each upload in `upload_log.json` and skips those files on rerun,
  so a failed batch can be rerun without duplicates
- Uploader: checks the channel for videos with the same original file name or title
  and skips them with a warning; `--allow-duplicate FILE` (repeatable) or `--force`
  uploads anyway, `--no-channel-check` skips the check
- Uploader: a logged upload whose video was deleted from YouTube is no longer
  treated as a duplicate; deleted videos still in the uploads list are ignored
- Go-live safeguards (both scripts): plain-language visibility ("PUBLIC immediately",
  "goes PUBLIC Sun Nov 22, 12:00 PM CST (in 1 day 3 hr)"); a y/N prompt before anything
  public, unlisted or scheduled (`--yes` to skip; refuses when not in a terminal);
  publishAt must be 15+ minutes away (`--min-lead`), re-checked before each upload.
  The updater now reads and shows every change before saving any.
- Uploader: a bare `filename` (and `thumbnail`) is found in `video_dir` or any folder
  under it, for dated folder trees; ambiguous names are an error listing the matches
- A publishAt that's too close can be moved to 15 minutes from now: asked y/N in a
  terminal, or automatically with `--fix-schedule` (both scripts)
- Examples list every supported field, with defaults and limits; a test keeps
  them in sync with the code
- Uploader: one failed video no longer aborts the batch; quota/limit errors stop it
- Uploader: sends `selfDeclaredMadeForKids: false` (was the read-only `madeForKids: True`)
- Uploader: supports `publishAt`, `recordingDate`, `madeForKids`, `language`; privacy
  defaults to private; tags trimmed and length-checked; `~` in `video_dir`
- Uploader: `--dry-run`
- Retry loop no longer keeps sleeping after a recovered error
- Updater: `--vids` now works (it was ignored)
- Updater: reads the video first and changes only the given fields; no longer wipes
  tags, language, localizations or status settings that weren't in the YAML
- Updater: no longer forces videos private or requires `publishAt`
- Updater: handles share links with `?si=` and watch/shorts/live URLs
- Updater: `--dry-run` shows old -> new without saving
- Removed `upload_video.py` (original sample); moved YAML samples to `examples/`;
  stopped tracking `vids/` and personal YAML files
- Added tests (`tests/`, fake YouTube service)

Version 0.2

- Added `draft_updater.py`
- Updated `README.md`
